{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3","id":1231627,"title":"My Judge's Ears Are Burning... (Ex3)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-01T12:35:42-07:00","id":1231627,"title":"My Judge's Ears Are Burning... (Ex3)","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1231614#post1231614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a similar vein: are there any other ways to decieve a Solar with Judge's Ear Technique?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1231616#post1231616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easiest way is to avoid speaking to them face-to-face.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bVance, as usual, is not wrong, but I'd like to take a moment to expand a bit on the options one has to defeat Judge's Ear Technique. This is far from comprehensive; I might even add to it later, particularly if good suggestions are made by others.<br /> <br /> Even putting aside the possibility of magic forcing Judge's Ear Technique into a roll-off, there are non-magical ways to defeat a Lawgiver with this admittedly-potent Solar Investigation Charm.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Method #1: Withholding the Statement</b><br /> <br /> \u200bA Lawgiver with Judge's Ear Technique can activate it to evaluate a given statement to determine falsehood. If there's no statement, the Lawgiver can't determine falsehood. If you have the option to not be there, <i>don't be there</i>. If you're forced into contact with the Lawgiver, refuse to speak. Take the fifth, as it were. If you are compelled to answer questions, write down the answers. If you must open your mouth, talk about anything <i>but </i>what he wants to hear.<br /> <br /> Of course, if he has ways of <i>making</i> you talk, or your silence would only serve to make you more suspicious, you can take advantage of...<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Method #2: The Activation Cost</b><br /> <br /> \u200bJudge's Ear Technique requires three motes of Essence to use. If he doesn't have three motes, a Lawgiver will have to resort to mundane means to differentiate truth from lies. This one requires creativity and a good poker face, so it's not as easy as Method #1, but it's still worth considering, especially if you've been forced into an audience, but have a way out after. Namely, the trick here is to <i>talk his Judge's Ear off</i>. An Essence 1 Solar only has enough divine resources to activate Judge's Ear Technique <i>fifteen times</i> without taking a break to recharge, and that's assuming they haven't spent any on social rolls, academic matters, or attunement costs, and have no interest in marshalling their divine power for the possibility of combat in the future.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso remember that just because Judge's Ear flags one of your statements as a lie, doesn't mean the Solar automatically knows what the truth is; telling him that the stolen shipment is buried in the palace courtyard, under the trees that make an &quot;X&quot; shape, only reveals the <i>one</i> place he <i>won't</i> find it.<br /> <br /> \u200bOf course, if he's just gonna keep you in his custody until he gets his answers, it's best to send...<br /> <br /> <b>Method #3: The Proxy</b><br /> <br /> \u200bIf the person speaking to the Solar doesn't know that what they're saying isn't true, Judge's Ear has no way of knowing the statement is false. A good tactic is to convince a third party of the truth of your words, and send <i>them</i> to go talk to the Solar for you.<br /> <br /> \u200bOf course, if none of those are quite the right fit for you, you might be...<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>Method #4: The Ebon Dragon</b><br /> <br /> \u200bThe biggest vulnerability of Judge's Ear Technique is that the user has to <i>decide </i>to activate it. If you must tell a lie, tell one that would pain the Solar to know is falsehood; if you must tell a truth, tell one so terrible that the Solar would never accept it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-01-2018, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T13:26:36-07:00","id":1231637,"title":"","content":"Don't forget phrasing. It is possible to phrase some things in such a way as to not tell a lie, but give the wrong impression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T13:37:52-07:00","id":1231642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1231637#post1231637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget phrasing. It is possible to phrase some things in such a way as to not tell a lie, but give the wrong impression.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's called a half-truth, and the interactions with those are noted specifically by the Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-01-2018, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T14:20:37-07:00","id":1231654,"title":"","content":"The wording on it though is:<br /> &quot;Her sense of lies is keen enough that if a character<br /> speaks in half-truths, she\u2019ll know which part of the<br /> statement is false.&quot;<br /> So, something which is technically correct I think still goes. Since there's no actual part of the statement which is false.<br /> (Actually, the way it says she knows which part of the statement is true seems a little odd, not sure how to read that: it'd make sense for a sentence containing both true and false things, but not really for half-truths. Well, maybe sometimes)<br /> <br /> For example, my Night Caste, Golden Hero (not his real name) met a very annoying Twilight, King Elf-Wise, who indignantly stated &quot;that's a lie&quot; every time my Night Caste lied. He doesn't understand diplomacy at all, or public relations.<br /> <br /> So I told him things like &quot;I was a slave&quot; and &quot;my father was a blacksmith.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now saying &quot;I was a slave&quot; is misleading, because he was a middle-class intellectual in a country where everyone was legally a slave to the Scarlet Empress. It's quite misleading. But there's no part of that statement that's actually false.<br /> Similarly, he didn't mention that his father was a successful businessman with 20 under-smiths under him, who only did the occasional bit of actual smithing himself, mostly he managed others. But &quot;he was a blacksmith&quot; doesn't really have any false parts to it.<br /> If Elf-Wise misinterprets these statements to think that Golden Hero is from a humble background, that's his own problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-01-2018, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T14:34:02-07:00","id":1231658,"title":"","content":"cant you also just write stuff down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T14:50:40-07:00","id":1231662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1231642#post1231642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's called a half-truth, and the interactions with those are noted specifically by the Charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much what Oz says. A half truth is leaving out reasonably known or assumed parts of the information with the intent of deception. For example, &quot;The defendant came across the victims while travelling and slew them.&quot; Reads a bit differently than, &quot;The defendant came across the victims while traveling and when they tried to rob him he killed them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T14:51:52-07:00","id":1231663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1231658#post1231658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cant you also just write stuff down?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that falls under the proxy or don't speak to them clause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T15:46:40-07:00","id":1231673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1231658#post1231658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cant you also just write stuff down?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed you can. It specifies a statement they <i>hear</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bI suppose deafening the Solar would also be a possibility, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T16:26:22-07:00","id":1231680,"title":"","content":"A word of caution on half-truths such as what Oz suggests, these can come down to Storyteller adjudication on the particulars of the context being used. To take his slave example, if the client state in question were not dejure slaves and were instead only defacto slaves, or they were simply \u201cslaves\u201d in the way Marxian doctrine views the prolitariate prior to revolution, then the ST could reasonably rule those outright falsehoods. As always, where there ar grey areas best check with/know how your ST views these kinds of things to avoid contentious conflicts between player and ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T17:00:01-07:00","id":1231685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1231680#post1231680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A word of caution on half-truths such as what Oz suggests, these can come down to Storyteller adjudication on the particulars of the context being used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've found that most often, &quot;magical lie detector&quot; abilities in RPG's simply come down to ST interpretation of truths and such. As a player, you might end up having to pause the game and argue for some time with the ST over why what your character said was &quot;technically true&quot; and shouldn't ping the NPC's lie detector. Likewise players might get annoyed when they use their character's magical lie detector on an NPC, are told the NPC isn't lying then discover later that the ST was very carefully treading the truth in order to nullify the player's ability.<br /> <br /> You might have some groups where players love arguing over what the definition of &quot;is&quot; is and whether a character's statement is a life, a half-truth or technically true, and whether it will ping someone's lie detector. But you'll have other groups (and I've played in them) with players who find the whole thing aggravating and get annoyed whenever the game comes to a halt so that a player and ST can argue over whether a given statement is true or not.<br /> <br /> Most often, just to save player aggravation and time, when someone decides to have a character lie to someone with a magical lie detector, rather than playing it out in character (and then arguing over whether things said by the player or ST are true or not), I prefer to have the character just make a a Manipulation roll to see how good they are at avoiding the whole truth while not tripping the lie detector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-01-2018, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T14:17:57-07:00","id":1232227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1231658#post1231658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">cant you also just write stuff down?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like it. JET only works on spoken statements and Linguistics can be pretty powerful, especially if your target doesn't have any Linguistics charms to oppose it.<br /> <br /> I'm now imagining a Judge quickly running out of patience as the person he's talking to refuses to communicate in any manner other than hastily scrawled sentences on the back of a napkin like a flippant teenager writing notes in class and the teacher getting pissed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T16:52:45-07:00","id":1232250,"title":"","content":"Not to mention how deliberately exploiting a gap in someone\u2019s truth-discerning skills is a great way to get everything you \u201csay\u201d slapped with a presumption of willful falsehood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T19:13:53-07:00","id":1232276,"title":"","content":"Assuming characters know that another has JET is also a bit dissonant IMO.<br /> <br /> Why would someone be so careful in speaking in half or technical truths?<br /> <br /> If you believe you're in the presence of a Lie Detecting God Arbiter, why do you think these technicalities matter? Who said he doesn`t know a written lie from a spoken one? A technical truth from intent?<br /> <br /> Seems some contrived positions are being assumed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T19:37:11-07:00","id":1232279,"title":"","content":"Depends on the circumstances of course. For example a thief-for-hire* or an assassin usually can't just go out saying they were out robbing someone or killing someone without repercussions. So if they were in a situation where the other party was known to have an almost perfect ability to spot lies they might very well try to figure out a way to say they were doing the job that doesn't explicitly say what they were doing. <br /> <br /> Of course nothing stopping a person with JET from also say making a check to see if the person is hiding something or trying to obfuscate their answers. Potentially resulting in, &quot;The person isn't lying to you, but you get the feeling there's something else they're concerned about on the subject.&quot;<br /> <br /> *I feel like there should be a name for that, but thief is the only thing coming to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T19:58:47-07:00","id":1232282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232276#post1232276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming characters know that another has JET is also a bit dissonant IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong, but JET isn't the only way to figure out that someone's lying. Many of the techniques that defeat Judge's Ear Technique (not being there, staying silent, sending a proxy, telling them something they overwhelmingly want to believe is true) can defeat mundane ways of spotting deception. Surely the Exalted RPG isn't the first to ever suggest that not letting yourself be questioned is a valid tactic to avoid getting caught in a lie?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232276#post1232276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you believe you're in the presence of a Lie Detecting God Arbiter, why do you think these technicalities matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because ultimately, said Arbiter is human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T20:04:13-07:00","id":1232286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232279#post1232279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*I feel like there should be a name for that, but thief is the only thing coming to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contract Burgular.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T20:16:31-07:00","id":1232289,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> <br /> <br /> Oh, I get the advice about avoiding questioning, but the general tone about the conversation seemd more toned how to avoid JET than how to not get caught in a lie. <br /> Like JET was a spell and someone encountered the specs for it.<br /> <br /> Just how it seemed to me, and that is where the dissonance comes through, for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T20:36:47-07:00","id":1232293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232289#post1232289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a><br /> <br /> Oh, I get the advice about avoiding questioning, but the general tone about the conversation seemd more toned how to avoid JET than how to not get caught in a lie.<br /> Like JET was a spell and someone encountered the specs for it.<br /> <br /> Just how it seemed to me, and that is where the dissonance comes through, for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that is kind of the point. I mean you could I suppose make multiple lies in a statement with the intent that if called out you confess to a lesser one, but the ability is supposed to just work provided magical things aren't brought into play to screw with it. <br /> <br /> Example of multi-lie: &quot;Last night? I was at a very close friend's house, whose identity I'd like to keep secret if possible, we played some darts and cards and I won all of them.&quot; When you were in fact over at a lover's house having an affair after you got slaughtered at a bunch of games. Leading to the intent of confessing to getting utterly obliterated at the game, as opposed to having the affair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T20:53:47-07:00","id":1232296,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a><br /> I get that the thread was made to discuss this, I'm just saying it doesn't jive like this for me. I'm speaking more of the nature of Charms, and in setting people's knowledge and experience of them. It is just dissonant and to contrary my understanding of the theme for people to have this attitude towards questioning by a Solar Judge.<br /> <br /> Considering the rarity of Solars themselves, then of Solars who have this Charm, the ephemeral and non distinct nature of Charms, discussion about how you should be writing down your answers to avoid the Solar Judge's magical discernment seems awkward. Even if you know he is a Solar, and one known to unerringly spot a lie.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying anyone is wrong, I'm just stating a style opinion of mine, that I know is just a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> From your example what I get from JET is that it would detect that you lied that you were at a &quot;friend's house&quot; (unless you truly consider your lover a friend, which is possible) and that you &quot;won all of them&quot;. The intent of your lie doesn't matter, it would indicate all lies and half truths in your statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 07-03-2018, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T21:05:43-07:00","id":1232298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232296#post1232296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3400_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3400\" data-vbnamecard=\"3400\">nalak42</a><br /> I get that the thread was made to discuss this, I'm just saying it doesn't jive like this for me. I'm speaking more of the nature of Charms, and in setting people's knowledge and experience of them. It is just dissonant and to contrary my understanding of the theme for people to have this attitude towards questioning by a Solar Judge.<br /> <br /> Considering the rarity of Solars themselves, then of Solars who have this Charm, the ephemeral and non distinct nature of Charms, discussion about how you should be writing down your answers to avoid the Solar Judge's magical discernment seems awkward. Even if you know he is a Solar, and one known to unerringly spot a lie.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying anyone is wrong, I'm just stating a style opinion of mine, that I know is just a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> From your example what I get from JET is that it would detect that you lied that you were at a &quot;friend's house&quot; (unless you truly consider your lover a friend, which is possible) and that you &quot;won all of them&quot;. The intent of your lie doesn't matter, it would indicate all lies and half truths in your statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not saying the intent would hide it. The goal in a multi lie is that the person would only pick up that the statement is a lie and being able to confess the truth to one lie as opposed to another. JET doesn't break down which parts of a statement are lies unless the person is telling a half-truth. Not necessarily indicating that multiple false statements in a single sentence would each get flags. <br /> <br /> Also I think the difference is your operating from the idea of an individual knowing their opposition is a solar using lie detecting magic. Whereas I'm at least operating from the perspective that the person isn't aware magic is involved and just thinks the person is freaking amazing at picking up on lies. I mean that is what JET is supposed to be an outgrowth of as opposed to a character with a crap sense motive/insight check in Dnd deciding to just start stocking up on ways to cast zone of truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T21:19:49-07:00","id":1232300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232298#post1232298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that is what JET is supposed to be an outgrowth of as opposed to a character with a crap sense motive/insight check in Dnd deciding to just start stocking up on ways to cast zone of truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the answer to &quot;I <i>just </i>think she is amazingly able to pick up when some in lying,&quot; isn't &quot;so I will lie in a <i>very specific </i>way to fool her as though I <i>know exactly </i>how her ability works.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T21:27:12-07:00","id":1232301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232298#post1232298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not saying the intent would hide it. The goal in a multi lie is that the person would only pick up that the statement is a lie and being able to confess the truth to one lie as opposed to another. JET doesn't break down which parts of a statement are lies unless the person is telling a half-truth. Not necessarily indicating that multiple false statements in a single sentence would each get flags. <br /> <br /> Also I think the difference is your operating from the idea of an individual knowing their opposition is a solar using lie detecting magic. Whereas I'm at least operating from the perspective that the person isn't aware magic is involved and just thinks the person is freaking amazing at picking up on lies. I mean that is what JET is supposed to be an outgrowth of as opposed to a character with a crap sense motive/insight check in Dnd deciding to just start stocking up on ways to cast zone of truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except the entire statement would trigger as false the first time. If any part of it was true that part would flag as true. So while each individual part doesnt get a flag as false. They do indirectly as they would of flagged as true if they had been true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T21:36:27-07:00","id":1232303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232300#post1232300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the answer to &quot;I <i>just </i>think she is amazingly able to pick up when some in lying,&quot; isn't &quot;so I will lie in a <i>very specific </i>way to fool her as though I <i>know exactly </i>how her ability works.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Half truths are exceptionally common, and confessing to a lesser crime is hardly an exceptionally specific method of lying. Just saying I'm not seeing the kind of scenario where an individual might decide to go for using a technical truth because they're afraid of getting called out on a lie as being something that requires the assumption that the person thinks magic will be used to call them out on the lie. To use a real world one I've seen a few times its considered more impressive and better for a person's image to be able to claim that they're a self-made rich person as opposed to inheriting fortune. Consequently I've seen several wealthy individuals claim themselves as self-made despite their startup company or money being from their family and also at a significantly higher amount than one would normally mean when they say self-made.*<br /> <br /> *This was at the least a lovely turn around in discussion than my sociology teacher talking about how the Bilderberg group secretly ran the world or the repeated subject of men just being inherently scum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T21:47:24-07:00","id":1232304,"title":"","content":"One more thing I feel is probably worth pointing out is that even magical lie-detecting isn't necessarily worth a damn if they don't have a way of proving you were lying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T21:51:38-07:00","id":1232305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232298#post1232298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not saying the intent would hide it. The goal in a multi lie is that the person would only pick up that the statement is a lie and being able to confess the truth to one lie as opposed to another. JET doesn't break down which parts of a statement are lies unless the person is telling a half-truth. Not necessarily indicating that multiple false statements in a single sentence would each get flags.<br /> <br /> Also I think the difference is your operating from the idea of an individual knowing their opposition is a solar using lie detecting magic. Whereas I'm at least operating from the perspective that the person isn't aware magic is involved and just thinks the person is freaking amazing at picking up on lies. I mean that is what JET is supposed to be an outgrowth of as opposed to a character with a crap sense motive/insight check in Dnd deciding to just start stocking up on ways to cast zone of truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that the Solar wouldn't know what part is a lie and what part is true;<br /> <br /> &quot;she\u2019ll know which part of the statement is false.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the part that is false is composed by more than one sentence, the JET user will the whole of the lie, in my view it is not restricted by the number or words or sentences.<br /> <br /> I think you are misunderstanding me. Because you speak as if I am the one acting like JET is a spell, when in fact I am saying exactly the opposite.<br /> <br /> I am arguing that there is no obvious magic (ephemeral and non distinct), so a target should act as they normally should when trying to bullshit someone ie act cool, look in the eye, be confident etc... Not trying to speak in technical truths or only agree to answer by writing.<br /> <br /> The fact that normal lying techniques are not effective against JET don't matter because 99,9999% of people don't even know someone can be so good at Investigation that they can operate under JET's paradigm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T21:56:31-07:00","id":1232307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232304#post1232304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more thing I feel is probably worth pointing out is that even magical lie-detecting isn't necessarily worth a damn if they don't have a way of proving you were lying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the usefulness of being able to tell a lie from truth is entirely circumstantial, I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T08:18:25-07:00","id":1232385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232276#post1232276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming characters know that another has JET is also a bit dissonant IMO.<br /> <br /> Why would someone be so careful in speaking in half or technical truths?<br /> <br /> If you believe you're in the presence of a Lie Detecting God Arbiter, why do you think these technicalities matter? Who said he doesn`t know a written lie from a spoken one? A technical truth from intent?<br /> <br /> Seems some contrived positions are being assumed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Twilight shouted &quot;liar!&quot; every time I told a straightforward lie, and didn't say anything when I said stuff that was technically true, so...<br /> (And, to reference Nalak42's point, I did point out that he could probably make Read Intentions rolls, but he failed them)<br /> <br /> But I do see your point. Generally speaking, it's not like PCs know how JET works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">One more thing I feel is probably worth pointing out is that even magical lie-detecting isn't necessarily worth a damn if they don't have a way of proving you were lying.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> This is a very good point. When my Night Caste was on trial and said he definitely didn't try and murder the Dawn, the Twilight kept saying he was lying... but he had no proof beyond &quot;I'm a Shining One and I say he's lying&quot; which isn't much good against the testimony of another Shining One.<br /> <br /> (It's also how international diplomacy generally works...)<br /> <br /> That's not to see it's not still pretty useful for the detector though. And it's certainly embaressing when people call out your lies.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T08:31:58-07:00","id":1232391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232385#post1232385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Twilight shouted &quot;liar!&quot; every time I told a straightforward lie, and didn't say anything when I said stuff that was technically true, so...<br /> (And, to reference Nalak42's point, I did point out that he could probably make Read Intentions rolls, but he failed them)<br /> <br /> But I do see your point. Generally speaking, it's not like PCs know how JET works.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be totally in favor of the character figuring out how to bypass JET, under those circumstances.<br /> <br /> The characters are interacting constantly, they are Circle mates (?).<br /> <br /> I can totally see the Night poking and prodding to understand how to get a lie through the Twilight. Seems like a fun part of narrating the group dynamics and helping establish the characters relationships.<br /> <br /> The Twilight's predictable righteousness (smugness?) and abraviseness pitted against the Night's relentless curiosity and resourcefulness. That is pretty classic.<br /> <br /> But all that would be lost if everytime someone encounters a Solar Investigator, they start communicating through notes or trying to have conversations through contrived musings about objective truths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T09:07:37-07:00","id":1232400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1231685#post1231685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer to have the character just make a a Manipulation roll to see how good they are at avoiding the whole truth while not tripping the lie detector.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone can make a contested roll against your Guile, which is derived from your Manipulation.<br /> <br /> If you can still use your Manipulation to conceal your lie, is Judge's Ears Technique actually accomplishing anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T09:15:32-07:00","id":1232401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232400#post1232400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone can make a contested roll against your Guile, which is derived from your Manipulation.<br /> <br /> If you can still use your Manipulation to conceal your lie, is Judge's Ears Technique actually accomplishing anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context AnubisXy is using it yes. What he\u2019s trying to do is create an objective measure to simulate the argument/adjudication of a player trying to skirt the edges of JET. The entire point is a method of resolution for people seeking to skirt/bypass JET in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:26:28-07:00","id":1232427,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a><br /> <br /> \u200bI don't think lie while bypassing JET is a valid objective of a Manipulation roll.<br /> <br /> You can have a Manipulation role with the objective of convincing someone of something. But not convince someone of something while lying and not trigger a lie detection Charm.<br /> <br /> So you can ask for a Manipulation roll to &quot;Convince Ben that his wife is dead without telling a single lie&quot;, but not to &quot;Tell Ben his wife is dead without triggering JET&quot;.<br /> <br /> On the first the narrative would be pointing out shes not amongst the gathered survivors of the raid, the palace has burned to the ground, nobody has seen her since, etc... Nudging Ben into taking what he believes are his conclusions.<br /> <br /> But there is no way to state a lie and not trigger JET. Not even deferring to system abstractions, as that would not make any sense, so it is not a valid application of the rules.<br /> <br /> PS. I would then use the Social Influence system, not just a Manipulation roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 07-04-2018, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T10:30:07-07:00","id":1232429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1232401#post1232401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the context AnubisXy is using it yes. What he\u2019s trying to do is create an objective measure to simulate the argument/adjudication of a player trying to skirt the edges of JET. The entire point is a method of resolution for people seeking to skirt/bypass JET in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much, yeah, it's just a resolution method.<br /> <br /> There are lots of RPGs out there with magical lie detectors (like Zone of Truth in D&amp;D). I've played (and ran) in quite a few sessions where gameplay would come to a halt as players or the ST would argue over whether a given phrase should constitute as a lie, and that generally wasn't much fun for anyone. Especially when a player was playing a conman who should have a silver tongue, but the player themself was not very good at twisting words around in real life.<br /> <br /> So if a character wants to mislead someone - make them draw the wrong conclusion without lying and triggering the magical lie detector, I just have the player or NPC make an appropriate roll ( Manipulation or Deception or Bluff or whatever is appropriate for the game system) to represent how good the character is at skirting the truth to mislead someone, rather than asking for the scene to be played out at the table and then have the individuals try to justify why what they said was or was not technically a lie and then let the ST try and come to a conclusion.<br /> <br /> As to whether Judge's Ear Technique accomplishes anything, most of the time people won't know that someone has JET and so they won't be trying to skirt the truth which makes it useful in 99% of situations. Further, even if someone dies know that a given person has JET and tries to mislead that person, JET still prevents that person from being able to outright lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-04-2018, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T18:07:42-07:00","id":1233125,"title":"","content":"Personally I think writing lies down to avoid JET is dangerous. Yes, it evades JET specifically, but I think it's extremely likely that charms that detect deliberate lies committed to text are at least <i>possible</i>. If they exist, writing down a lie is actually more dangerous than speaking it because it can be checked later. (Presumably such charms would have limitations for just this reason, to balance out the power and utility of being able to check a statement at any point, but it's still clearly something that someone could have in some form.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 07-08-2018, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T21:07:50-07:00","id":1233136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1233125#post1233125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think writing lies down to avoid JET is dangerous. Yes, it evades JET specifically, but I think it's extremely likely that charms that detect deliberate lies committed to text are at least <i>possible</i>. If they exist, writing down a lie is actually more dangerous than speaking it because it can be checked later. (Presumably such charms would have limitations for just this reason, but it's still clearly something that someone could have.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a good follow up charm in the Investigation tree, or a neat Linguistics charm with an Investigation prerequisite.<br /> <br /> I could even see acfew stunts using it:<br /> &quot;You see here, where the ink pools on this letter A halfway, he did not originally mean to write Aunt Maude, but instead Assassin.&quot; Or some other crazy thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T21:35:00-07:00","id":1233138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cryo-Seraph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1231627-my-judge-s-ears-are-burning-ex3?p=1233136#post1233136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a good follow up charm in the Investigation tree, or a neat Linguistics charm with an Investigation prerequisite.<br /> <br /> I could even see acfew stunts using it:<br /> &quot;You see here, where the ink pools on this letter A halfway, he did not originally mean to write Aunt Maude, but instead Assassin.&quot; Or some other crazy thing</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds <a href=\"https://www.smbc-comics.com/comic/holmes\" target=\"_blank\">legit.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}